It should format short arguments with an empty body
{% block 'hero', heading: heading, content: captured_content %}{% endblock %}

It should format short arguments with a non-empty body
{% block 'hero', heading: heading %}
  <h2>{{ heading }}</h2>
{% endblock %}

It should format long arguments with an empty body
printWidth: 1
{% block 'featured-heading',
  heading: section.settings.heading,
  alignment: section.settings.alignment,
%}{% endblock %}

It should format long arguments with a non-empty body
printWidth: 1
{% block 'featured-heading',
  heading: section.settings.heading,
  alignment: section.settings.alignment,
%}
  Heading
{% endblock %}

It should wrap arguments when the closing delimiter does not fit
printWidth: 40
{% block 'x',
  a: b,
  c: d,
%}{% endblock %}
